<pdd-reason>Native macOS parity for the approved Ubuntu browsing story.</pdd-reason>
<pdd-dependency>model_rust.prompt</pdd-dependency>
Implement src/native.rs using Rust and native AppKit via Objective-C. main.rs is
separately mapped by main_rust.prompt; keep both interfaces compatible.
R1 (MUST): Resizable window, sidebar Places/Favorites/Recent/Frequent with full
path tooltips, always-visible path field, back/forward/up/refresh/star/copy.
Native multi-select table with Name/Modified/Size sorting and double-click/Return.
R2 (MUST): Command+L/D/C/Shift+C/R, back/forward Command+[/], Command+Up.
Path entry's native text copy MUST NOT be hijacked. Copy selection/current path
to NSPasteboard; open documents with NSWorkspace URLs, never a shell.
R3 (MUST): Context menus and local-directory drag/drop for favorites, URL export.
Unavailable favorites removable. Drops MUST NOT move/delete or execute data.
R4 (MUST): Silver/Midnight/Aurora/Automatic, validated NSImage background picker,
remove background, shortcuts and clear-history menus. Invalid image retains prior.
R5 (MUST): Main-thread AppKit, responsive single-worker-per-window scanning and stale result
rejection; periodic metadata-only refresh without visits. Visible errors.
R6 (MUST NOT): Telemetry, unsolicited network access, content inspection or
source document mutations. Explicit SMB connections are allowed under R10.
R7 (MUST): Native fixture mode uses temporary documents/preferences, exercises
real controls, actual clipboard (restored afterward), callbacks, persistence,
selection, appearance, drops, navigation and stale results; do not claim physical
drag/default-app opening unless manually observed.
R8 (MUST): Participate in native macOS window tiling and Apple's documented
hotkeys for the OS version in use: Fill, Center, half-screen positioning, Return
to Previous Size and supported multi-window arrangements. Preserve native
dispatch with path-editor or file-list focus; MUST NOT reinterpret tiling keys
as browsing/text actions, mutate browsing state/documents, override existing
Command browsing shortcuts, or require global remapping/third-party tools.
Keep controls usable at native permitted tiled sizes and avoid unnecessary
window-sizing restrictions that prevent supported layouts. Desktop Fill is
not full screen; do not invent shortcuts Apple marks unavailable or emulate
unsupported OS features. Independent acceptance and version-specific hotkey
matrix: user_stories/story__macos_window_tiling.md.
Register the real NSApplication.windowsMenu so AppKit supplies its own tiling
items/key equivalents. Submenu wrappers have no command action so native
validation/key dispatch works. Do not synthesize a replacement window manager. Keep a
compact usable minimum size/layout; verify OS-provided entries and window frames.
R9 (MUST): Provide native AppKit tabs, File > New Tab and Command–T, Close Tab /
Command–W (last closes window), and Control–Tab/Control–Shift–Tab. Tabs retain
independent folder/history/selection/path draft/sorting, sharing favorites,
visits/appearance and one
scan worker through model TabbedBrowser. Tab switches MUST NOT increment visits,
overwrite another tab's view with late results, mutate documents, or break
native text editing. Native tab strip, add/close controls stay usable when tiled.
Acceptance: user_stories/story__macos_tabs.md. Restore saved folder order,
active index and independent sorts through the model. Verify actual restored
NSTabView items and header callbacks with synthetic native preferences. Keep a
separate saved-tab fixture so failures of OS tiling do not hide tab evidence;
the existing full native/tiling fixture remains required and must still fail
when its assertions do not pass. Run graphical fixture processes sequentially.
Retain native_desktop.rs and native_tiling_test.rs as independent acceptance
helpers. Geometry tests dispatch real OS actions from asynchronous outer-event-
loop steps, assert complete frames (with native-margin tolerance), actual field-
editor/list responder identities, non-fullscreen state and unchanged browse
state. Key-equivalent synthesis is not a claim of physical keyboard coverage.

R10 (MUST): Extend the always-visible full editable path bar to accept smb://
URLs, and provide Go > Connect to Server… / Command–K with an address dialog.
Use native NetFS/NetAuth with optional URL username and null password, allowing
macOS authentication/share picker and saved Keychain credentials. Never read
Keychain secrets or store passwords. Reject embedded passwords, query/fragment,
invalid hosts/schemes and escaping subpaths without echoing URL contents; remove
rejected URL text from the field. Accept server-only, share and nested-folder
URLs, escaped spaces, Unicode and IP hosts. Use actual mountpoints returned by
macOS, never a guessed /Volumes name; open first returned point if multiple.
Show its POSIX subfolder path in the bar/list and retain ordinary local typing,
folder opening, history, selection and favorites. One outstanding mount worker
keeps NetFS off the main UI thread (Foundation parsing there is permitted);
AppKit stays on main. Poll completion via the timer and Browser connection token;
late results after local navigation or tab changes MUST NOT navigate the view.
Report busy/cancel/failure visibly, preserving prior listing/history/preferences.
No live-server/password fixtures. Test native timer delivery with injected
synthetic mount results separately from real authentication acceptance.

R11 (MUST): File > New Window / Command–N creates a separate visible NSWindow
with one tab at the current successful folder, preserving the source window's
selection, tabs, history and path draft. Independent window contexts own their
TabbedBrowser, display/widgets, render/tab guards, displayed path, scan worker,
connection receiver and timer. Route delegate/table callbacks to their owning
window; shared menu actions route to the focused live window. Restore context
after nested callbacks; background timer work must not steal command focus.
Shared favorites, visits and appearance propagate between windows before saves
without overwriting their independent folder/tab/sort/session data. Refresh
shared UI without erasing drafts. Closing any window invalidates its timer,
drops its browser/connection receiver and leaves other windows usable, including
when the original closes. Command–W closes a tab or its last tab's window;
closing the last window leaves New Window available. Command–Q quits normally.
Retain last-saved single-window tab-session persistence; all-window restoration
is not required. Never use personal preferences/documents in fixtures. Test
real visible NSWindows, focused menu routing, independent tabs/folders/drafts/
selection/connection replies, shared preferences, original/secondary close and
New Window after last close. Keep existing tiling/SMB/tab tests intact.
Acceptance: user_stories/story__macos_new_windows.md.
